  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohd Yameen vs State Of U.P. And 2 Others on 24 July, 2025 Author: Manoj Kumar Gupta Bench: Manoj Kumar Gupta High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2025:Ahc:121817-Db Court No. - 21 Case :- Writ - C No. - 17466 of 2025 Petitioner :- Mohd Yameen Respondent :- State Of U.P. And 2 Others Counsel for Petitioner :- Mashaluddin Shah,Sarvesh Yadav",
    "facts": "The instant petition has been filed with grievance that the petitioner, who is having a valid license under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 for working as a whole-seller, distributor, retailer of meat, is not being permitted to carry on his business. The petitioner has accordingly prayed for a direction to the respondent to decide his representation filed in this behalf.",
    "arguments": "2. Learned Standing Counsel has placed on record the instructions from District Magistrate, Firozabad in which it is admitted that the petitioner's firm was granted License No. 12724999000347 dated 6.4.2025 by the Central Licensing Authority, New Delhi and the said license is valid upto 5.4.2026. 3. Learned counsel for the petitioner admits that since after filing of the writ petition, there has been no obstruction in carrying on of business by the petitioner.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2. Learned Standing Counsel has placed on record the instructions from District Magistrate, Firozabad in which it is admitted that the petitioner's firm was granted License No. 12724999000347 dated 6.4.2025 by the Central Licensing Authority, New Delhi and the said license is valid upto 5.4.2026. 3. Learned counsel for the petitioner admits that since after filing of the writ petition, there has been no obstruction in carrying on of business by the petitioner.",
